[#:seon.task{:name "file-edit-tools-bypass-write-back"
             :plan "`my.edit/form!`, exact! and lines! let an agent edit source files, against 'files are the write-back of accepted entities, not the working medium' (dogfood c8b; root decided removal). Retire my.edit, seon.edit, seon.edit.jvm and their schemas (bundle B4, delete-only). Read `my.edit/exact!`, `my.edit/lines!` and `docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-report-2026-09-26.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "edit-hook-budgets-need-owner-numbers"
             :plan "Edit-hook budgets (function at most 40 lines, a namespace over 800 lines may only shrink, short docstrings, no dated rulings in comments): the exact numbers need the owner's OK before the hook enforces them. Done when the owner rules the numbers and the hook refuses each violation with a fix, with a regression per budget. Read `my.edit/exact!`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "exact-has-no-digest-for-a-file-over-eight-kilobytes"
             :plan "`my.edit/exact!` and `my.edit/form!` require the whole file's `:my.edit/expected-digest`, but `my.fs/read` caps every window at 8,192 bytes whatever `:my.fs/max-bytes` asks (65,536 or 4,000,000 on the 54,827-byte src/seon/sci/kernel.clj answered `:my.fs/bytes-read 8192`, `:eof? false`, no `:my.fs/digest`), and a stale-digest refusal does not name the current digest. Observed (Wave A A5, default 35e95e7b3, 2026-10-09) had to hash the file with java.security.MessageDigest in SCI to edit it. Done when an agent gets a file's whole digest from one Seon call (the stale refusal answering it, or `my.fs/stat`), with a regression on a file over 8 KB."}]
